.TH Objectspace 1 "@DATE@" "Objectspace @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
osd \- Objectspace for scripts: objects, messages and questions, in plain text
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B osd open
.IR PATH ...
.br
.B osd get
.I PATH NAME
.br
.B osd set
.I PATH
.RI ' NAME = VALUE ;...'
.br
.B osd create
.I FOLDER CLASS TITLE
.br
.B osd shadow
.I PATH FOLDER
.br
.B osd say
.RB [ \-\-stay ]
.I TEXT
.br
.B osd notify
.I TITLE
.RI [ TEXT ]
.br
.B osd ask
.I TEXT
.RI [ BUTTON ...]
.br
.B osd folder
.br
.B osd selection
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B osd
lets scripts work with Objectspace's objects, as REXX scripts did on OS/2. Its
output is plain text, one value a line; it exits with 0 when it worked,
1 when it did not (with a message on standard error).
.TP
.B open
Opens each object as a double click would: a folder's window, a file in
its program, a program.
.TP
.B get
Prints a property's value (for example
.BR "osd get ~/Work icon_font" ).
.TP
.B set
Sets properties with a setup string. The path may also be
.BI class: NAME
(every object of a class) or
.BI type: MIME
(every file of a type).
.TP
.B create
Makes an object of a class (OsdFolder, OsdDataFile, ...) in a folder and
prints its path.
.TP
.B shadow
Makes a shadow of an object in a folder and prints its path, or its
address (\fBvobj:\fIID\fR) when the folder keeps shadows centrally.
.TP
.B say
Shows a message at the bottom of the desktop; with
.B \-\-stay
it stays until clicked.
.TP
.B notify
Shows a notification.
.TP
.B ask
Shows an Objectspace dialog with the buttons given (OK if none) and prints the one
chosen; exits with 1 if it was closed without a choice.
.TP
.B folder
Prints the folder the script or Command Prompt was started from
.RB ( $OSD_FOLDER ).
.TP
.B selection
Prints the paths of the objects selected in the active folder window
(else on the desktop).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OSD_FOLDER
Set by Command prompt here: the folder.
.TP
.BR OSD_OBJECT ", " OSD_PATH ", " OSD_EVENT
Set for programs an object's actions start.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR osdctl (1),
.BR osd-terminal (1),
.BR osd-shell (1)
